REGENT OF MUARA ENIM

REGENT OF MUARA ENIM

PROVINCE OF SOUTH SUMATRA

REGIONAL REGULATION OF MUARA ENIM REGENCY

NUMBER 5 OF 2023

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF MUARA ENIM,

Considering

a. that to ensure the Protection of Women and Children in accordance with their dignity and to guarantee their right to life in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination and to obtain Protection from violence and other violations, legal certainty is necessary;

b. that to provide legal certainty in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children and to carry out mandatory regional government affairs, regulation in the form of a Regional Regulation is necessary;

c. that based on the considerations referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children;

In View of

1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 28 of 1959 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 3 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Level I Region of South Sumatra and Emergency Law Number 16 of 1955 concerning Amendment to Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 3 of 1950 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 70, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1814);

(2)

3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3277);

4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

5. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection to Become Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);

6. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

7. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);

8. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times, most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 238, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6841);

(3)

9. Government Regulation Number 78 of 2021 concerning Special Protection for Children (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2021 Number 174, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6704);

10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 11 of 2011 concerning Policy on Child-Friendly Regency/City Development;

11. Regional Regulation Number 14 of 2014 concerning Free Legal Aid (Regional Gazette of Muara Enim Regency of 2014 Number 014);

12. Regional Regulation Number 9 of 2020 concerning Implementation of Child-Friendly Regency (Regional Gazette of 2020 Number 9);

13. Regional Regulation of Muara Enim Regency Number 2 of 2022 concerning Gender Mainstreaming (Regional Gazette of Muara Enim Regency of 2021 Number 2);

With Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF MUARA ENIM REGENCY
and

THE REGENT OF MUARA ENIM

HAS DECIDED:

To Establish: REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

text:
Pasal 2

Penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak berdasarkan asas:

a. kepentingan terbaik bagi perempuan dan Anak;
b. keadilan gender dan kesetaraan gender;
c. kearifan lokal;
d. penegakan dan kepastian hukum.
e. non diskriminasi;
f. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup, dan perkembangan; g. penghargaan terhadap pendapat Anak; dan
h. penegakan dan kepastian hukum.

translated_text:
Article 2

The implementation of Women's and Children's Protection is based on the principles of:

a. best interests for women and Children;
b. gender justice and gender equality;
c. local wisdom;
d. law enforcement and legal certainty.
e. non-discrimination;
f. the right to life, survival, and development; g. respect for the opinion of Children; and
h. law enforcement and legal certainty.

This excerpt sits under: CHAPTER I

text:
Pasal 3

Peraturan Daerah ini bertujuan:

a. menjamin terpenuhinya hak perempuan dan Anak di Kabupaten;

(8)

b. sebagai pedoman bagi Daerah dalam perencanaan, kebijakan dan strategi Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;

c. melindungi dan mencegah perempuan dan Anak dari tindakan, keputusan dan kebijakan yang melanggar hak perempuan dan Anak;

d. meningkatkan peran dan nilai kearifan lokal serta peranan adat dalam Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;

e. sebagai payung hukum bagi perangkat daerah yang membidangi perlindungan perempuan dan anak dalam rangka memberi bantuan pendampingan korban perempuan dan anak.

translated_text:
Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:

a. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and Children in the Regency;

(8)

b. serve as a guideline for the Region in planning, policies and strategies for the Protection of Women and Children;

c. protect and prevent women and Children from actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of women and Children;

d. enhance the role and value of local wisdom as well as the role of customs in the Protection of Women and Children;

e. serve as a legal umbrella for regional apparatus in charge of the protection of women and children in order to provide assistance and support to victims of women and children.

text:
Pasal 4

Ruang lingkup pengaturan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak meliputi:

a. perlindungan perempuan;
b. perlindungan Anak;
c. pemenuhan hak Anak;
d. peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan;
e. sistem data gender dan Anak, data terpilah perempuan dan anak, dan penguatan kelembagaan Pengarusutamaan Gender melalui Perencanaan dan Penganggaran Responsif Gender;
f. peran serta masyarakat; dan
g. pembinaan, pengawasan, pendampingan.

translated_text:
Article 4

The scope of regulation of the Protection of Women and Children includes:

a. protection of women;
b. protection of Children;
c. fulfillment of the rights of Children;
d. improvement of the quality of life of women;
e. gender and Children data system, disaggregated data on women and children, and strengthening of Gender Mainstreaming institutions through Gender Responsive Planning and Budgeting;
f. community participation; and
g. guidance, supervision, support.

text:
Pasal 5

( 1) Dalam rangka meningkatkan kualitas hid up perempuan, pemerintah daerah bertanggung jawab:

a. menghormati dan menjamin hak perempuan tanpa diskriminasi sesuai dengan harkat dan martabat kemanusiaan;
b. melaksanakan Pengarusutamaan Gender di Kabupaten; c. membentuk pokja Pengarusutamaan Gender di Daerah; d. meningkatkan Pemberdayaan Perempuan dalam peran, kualitas dan kemampuan dibidang (9)
1. politik;
2. hukum;
3. sosial;
4. ekonomi; dan
5. budaya.
e. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan Pemberdayaan Perempuan di Kabupaten.
(2) Tanggungjawab Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam upaya peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh perangkat daerah sesuai dengan tugas dan fungsinya.

translated_text:
Article 5

( 1) In order to improve the quality of life of women, the regional government is responsible for:

a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity;
b. implementing Gender Mainstreaming in the Regency; c. establishing a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region; d. improving Women's Empowerment in terms of role, quality and capacity in the fields of (9)
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social;
4. economy; and
5. culture.
e. strengthening and developing institutions providing Women's Empowerment services in the Regency.
(2) The responsibility of the Regency Government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

text:
Pasal 6

Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam bidang politik sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf d angka 1 meliputi:

a. melaksanakan sosialisasi untuk meningkatkan partisipasi politik perempuan dalam pemilihan umum;
b. melaksanakan program yang mendorong tingkat keterlibatan perempuan dalam proses politik dan jabatan publik;
c. melakukan fasilitasi pengembangan diri perempuan dalam berorganisasi, berserikat dan berkumpul; dan
d. melibatkan perempuan dalam pengambilan keputusan yang menyangkut kepentingan perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 6

Efforts to improve the role, quality and capacity of women in the field of politics as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 1 include:

a. conducting socialization to increase women's political participation in general elections;
b. implementing programs that encourage the level of women's involvement in political processes and public positions;
c. facilitating women's self-development in organizing, associating and assembling; and
d. involving women in decision-making concerning women's interests.

text:
Pasal 8

Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam biclang sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf cl angka 3 meliputi:

a. peningkatan pengetahuan dan keterampilan untuk mendorong pemenuhan pendidikan sesuai dengan potensi yang dimiliki; b. peningkatan dan pemenuhan kualitas kesehatan terhaclap perempuan;
c. peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan tentang perencanaan keluarga mandiri, sehat dan sejahtera termasuk akses layanan konsultasi dan pencatatan perkawinan;
d. peningkatan kesadaran perempuan terhadap dampak pernikahan dini;
e. memfasilitasi dan mengupayakan pelestarian adat istiadat dan pengembangan ilmu pengetahuan, teknologi, seni dan budaya untuk kemajuan perempuan;
f. melakukan peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan perempuan terhadap perencanaan keluarga mandiri, sehat clan sejahtera; g. melakukan program dalam menurunkan angka kematian ibu melahirkan; clan
h. menclorong pembentukan organisasi perempuan di Kabupaten.

translated_text:
Article 8

Efforts to improve the role, quality and capacity of women in the social field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 3 include:

a. increasing knowledge and skills to encourage the fulfillment of education in accordance with existing potential; b. improving and fulfilling the quality of health for women;
c. increasing awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;
d. increasing women's awareness of the impacts of early marriage;
e. facilitating and pursuing the preservation of customs and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;
f. increasing women's awareness and knowledge of independent, healthy and prosperous family planning; g. implementing programs to reduce maternal mortality rates; and
h. encouraging the formation of women's organizations in the Regency.

text:
Pasal 9

Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam bidang ekonomi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf d angka 4 meliputi:

(11)

a. melaksanakan program, kegiatan, pelatihan untuk peningkatan keterampilan dan keahlian perempuan dalam rangka mewujudkan peningkatan kesejahteraan perempuan;

b. fasilitasi penguatan modal usaha bagi perempuan yang memiliki ekonomi lemah;

c. pemasaran produk hasil usaha perempuan yang memiliki ekonomi lemah;

d. pelatihan pengembangan kemampuan perempuan melalui pemberdayaan ekonomi keluarga prasejahtera; dan

e. pelatihan kewirausahaan kepada perempuan secara komprehensif.

translated_text:
Article 9

Efforts to improve the role, quality and capacity of women in the field of economy as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter d number 4 include:

(11)

a. implementing programs, activities, training to improve women's skills and expertise in order to realize the improvement of women's welfare;

b. facilitating the strengthening of business capital for women with weak economies;

c. marketing products from businesses of women with weak economies;

d. training for the development of women's capacity through economic empowerment of pre-prosperous families; and

e. comprehensive entrepreneurship training for women.

text:
Pasal 10

(1) Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam upaya Perlindungan perempuan bertanggungjawab:

a. menetapkan dan menyelenggarakan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan perempuan;
b. melakukan upaya pencegahan terjadinya tindak Kekerasan terhadap perempuan termasuk tindak pidana perdagangan orang;
c. meningkatkan efektivitas layanan terhadap perempuan korban tindak Kekerasan;
d. meningkatkan upaya perlindungan terhadap tenaga kerja perempuan;
e. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan perlindungan perempuan;
f. melakukan kerjasama dengan Pemerintah, Pemerintah Daerah lainnya, pihak swasta, dunia usaha dan/atau Lembaga Swadaya Masyarakat dalam upaya pencegahan terjadinya tindak Kekerasan terhadap perempuan;
g. melibatkan peran aktif keluarga, pemuka adat, pemuka agama, masyarakat, dan lembaga dibidang perlindungan perempuan.

(12)

(2) Tanggungjawab Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam upaya perlindungan perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh perangkat daerah sesuai dengan tugas dan fungsinya serta dapat berkoordinasi dengan instansi terkait.

translated_text:
Article 10

(1) The Regency Government in efforts to Protect women is responsible for:

a. establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women;
b. making efforts to prevent acts of Violence against women including criminal acts of trafficking in persons;
c. improving the effectiveness of services for women victims of acts of Violence;
d. improving efforts to protect female workers;
e. strengthening and developing institutions providing women's protection services;
f. cooperating with the Government, other Regional Governments, the private sector, the business community and/or Non-Governmental Organizations in efforts to prevent acts of Violence against women;
g. involving the active role of families, customary leaders, religious leaders, communities, and institutions in the field of women's protection.

(12)

(2) The responsibility of the Regency Government in efforts to protect women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions and may coordinate with relevant agencies.

text:
Pasal 11

Dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya tindak Kekerasan terhadap perempuan, Pemerintah Kabupaten :

a. menyelenggarakan sosialisasi, mengenai pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dengan mengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat, budaya, agama dan organisasi kemasyarakatan;
b. membangun jejaring dan kerja sama dengan aparatur penegak hukum, aparatur pemerintah, perguruan tinggi dan berbagai Lembaga Swadaya Masyarakat yang bergerak dan/ atau peduli terhadap perempuan dan anak korban Kekerasan;
c. menyediakan fasilitas umum yang nyaman dan aman untuk perempuan;
d. membentuk Unit Pelayanan Teknis Daerah Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak serta menyediakan sekretariat Unit Pelayanan Teknis Daerah Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak.

translated_text:
Article 11

In order to prevent acts of Violence against women, the Regency Government:

a. conducts socialization on the prevention of violence against women by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. builds networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various Non-Governmental Organizations engaged in and/or concerned with women and children victims of Violence;
c. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women;
d. establishes a Regional Technical Service Unit for the Protection of Women and Children and provides a secretariat for the Regional Technical Service Unit for the Protection of Women and Children.

text:
Pasal 12

( 1) Perlindungan perempuan korban tindak Kekerasan dilaksanakan melalui layanan terpadu.

(2) Pemberian layanan terpadu terhadap perempuan korban tindak Kekerasan sebagiamana dimaksud pada ayat (1) menggunakan prinsip:

a. responsif gender;
b. non diskriminasi;

(13)

c. hubungan setara dan menghormati;

d. menjaga kerahasiaan;

e. memberi rasa arnan dan nyarnan;

f. menghargai perbedaan individu;

g. tidak menghakimi;

h. menghormati pilihan dan keputusan korban;

1. peka terhadap latar belakang dan kondisi korban dan pemakaian bahasa yang sesuai dan dimengerti oleh korban;

J. cepat dan sederhana;

k. empati; dan

1. pemenuhan hak perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 12

( 1) Protection of women victims of acts of Violence is carried out through integrated services.

(2) The provision of integrated services for women victims of acts of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) uses the principles of:

a. gender responsive;
b. non-discrimination;

(13)

c. equal and respectful relations;

d. maintaining confidentiality;

e. providing a sense of security and comfort;

f. respecting individual differences;

g. non-judgmental;

h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;

1. sensitive to the background and condition of victims and the use of appropriate language understood by victims;

J. fast and simple;

k. empathy; and

1. fulfillment of women's rights.

text:
Pasal 13

Bentuk layanan terpadu terhadap perempuan korban tindak kekerasan meliputi:

a. penanganan pengaduan; ·
b. pelayanan kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. pendampingan korban, penegakan dan bantuan hukum; dan e. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.

translated_text:
Article 13

Forms of integrated services for women victims of acts of violence include:

a. handling complaints; ·
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. victim support, enforcement and legal assistance; and e. repatriation and social reintegration.

text:
Pasal 14

Layanan terpadu penanganan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 13 huruf a dilaksanakan oleh:

a. Rumah Sakit, Pusat Kesehatan Masyarakat dan sarana pelayanan kesehatan lainnya;
b. Unit Pelaksana Teknis Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak; c. Rumah Perlindungan Trauma Center,
d. Women crisis centre;
e. Badan Penasehat Pembinaan Dan Pelestarian Perkawinan; f. Kepolisian;
g. Kejaksaan;
h. Pengadilan;
i. Kementerian Agama; dan/ atau
J. Lembaga Bantuan Hukum.

translated_text:
Article 14

Integrated complaint handling services as referred to in Article 13 letter a shall be carried out by:

a. Hospitals, Community Health Centers and other health service facilities;
b. Technical Implementation Unit for the Protection of Women and Children; c. Shelter Trauma Center,
d. Women crisis centre;
e. Marriage Guidance, Development and Preservation Advisory Board; f. Police;
g. Prosecutor's Office;
h. Courts;
i. Ministry of Religious Affairs; and/ or
J. Legal Aid Institutions.

text:
Pasal 17

(1) Rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 13 huruf c ditujukan untuk memulihkan dan mengembangkan kemampuan terhadap perempuan korban tindak Kekerasan yang mengalami disfungsi sosial untuk dapat melaksanakan fungsi sosialnya dalam masyarakat secara wajar.

(2) Rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi pelayanan:

a. motivasi dan diagnosis psikososial;
b. perawatan dan pengasuhan;
c. pelatihan vokasional dan pembinaan kewirausahaan; d. bimbingan mental spiritual;
e. bimbingan fisik;
f. bim bing an sosial dan konseling psikososial;
g. pelayanan aksesibilitas;
h. bantuan dan asistensi sosial;
1. bimbingan resosialisasi;
J. bimbingan lanjut; dan/atau
k. rujukan.
(3) Penyelenggaraan pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) diselenggarakan oleh:
a. perangkat daerah yang mempunyai tugas dan fungsi dibidang sosial;
b. perangkat daerah yang membidangi Pemberdayaan Perempuan, dan dapat bekerjasama dengan pusat pelayanan terpadu, women crisis centre atau organisasi kemasyarakatan bidang sosial yang telah ada; atau
c. Kementerian Agama.

translated_text:
Article 17

(1) Social rehabilitation as referred to in Article 13 letter c is aimed at restoring and developing the capacity of women victims of acts of violence who experience social dysfunction to be able to perform their social functions in society normally.

(2) Social rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes services:

a. motivation and psychosocial diagnosis;
b. care and nurturing;
c. vocational training and entrepreneurship development; d. mental spiritual guidance;
e. physical guidance;
f. social guidance and psychosocial counseling;
g. accessibility services;
h. social assistance and aid;
1. resocialization guidance;
J. follow-up guidance; and/or
k. referral.
(3) The provision of services as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be organized by:
a. regional apparatus having duties and functions in the social field;
b. regional apparatus responsible for Women's Empowerment, and may cooperate with integrated service centers, women crisis centres or existing social community organizations; or
c. Ministry of Religious Affairs.

text:
Pasal 18

(1) Pelayanan konseling sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 17 ayat (2) huruf a bertujuan:

a. membantu perempuan korban tindak kekerasan mengenali permasalahannya dan menemukan cara-cara yang efektif untuk mengatasinya sendiri;
b. memberdayakan perempuan korban tindak kekerasan untuk menentukan masa depannya;
