Article 84

(1) The Regency Government is obliged to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence.

(2) Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:

a. guidelines and standards for fulfillment;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. provision of facilities;
d. monitoring; and
e. evaluation.
(3) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) is in order to realize the objectives of protection for women and children victims of violence in accordance with minimum service standards implemented by the agency responsible for Women and Child Protection.
(4) The agency responsible for Women and Child Protection is obliged to report periodically to the Regent regarding the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence.
